### 2. Deep Root Cause Analysis (RCA)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Webcam Frames Stream to SmartSpectra C-API"] --> B["Facial ROI capillary detection"]
    B --> C["10–15s Lock: Pulse Rate (80.25 bpm) ✅"]
    B --> D["30s Rolling Window: Breathing Rate"]
    B --> E["60s Continuous RR-Intervals: HRV (RMSSD)"]
    
    F["Head Movement / Angle Shift (Code 16 / Code 7)"] -.->|Interrupts Signal| D
    F -.->|Resets 60s IBI Buffer| E
    
    D -->|Confidence < 45 or stable=false| G["Filtered by Quality Gate: 'No signal'"]
    E -->|Confidence < 50 or stable=false| H["Filtered by Quality Gate: 'Not measured'"]
```

1. **Protobuf Telemetry Quality Gating** ([metrics.ts](file:///Users/shivam/work/hotel-coach/src/services/vitals/metrics.ts#L132-L163)):
   - In `applyQualityGate()`:
     - `pulseValid`: requires `confidence >= 40` and `pulseStable === true` (achieved: 80.25 bpm).
     - `breathingValid`: requires `confidence >= 45` and `breathingStable === true`.
     - `hrvValid`: requires `confidence >= 50` and `hrvStable === true`.
2. **The 60-Second Inter-Beat Interval (IBI) Ceiling**:
   - The calibration window is exactly 60 seconds.
   - If any portion of the 60 seconds experiences validation drops (`ValidationCode != 0`, e.g. face angle, speaking, or movement), the continuous window required for HRV is broken.
   - Under the strict project engineering rule **"Never fabricate vitals"**, any missing or low-confidence metrics evaluate to `null`, correctly displaying `"No signal"` and `"Not measured"`.

#### How to get a "Good" rating with all 3 metrics:
- Retake the baseline, sit upright with your face centered in the guide oval.
- Keep your head still, look straight ahead, and breathe naturally for the full 60 seconds without speaking.

