### 3. Comprehensive Resource Release Architecture

To ensure that **camera, microphone, audio contexts, worker threads, and native SDK sessions are released in ANY scenario** (app close, window close, reload, crash, or unhandled exception), we implemented:

1. **Global Media Lifecycle Manager** ([mediaLifecycle.ts](file:///Users/shivam/work/hotel-coach/src/utils/mediaLifecycle.ts)):
   - Intercepts `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia` across the entire application to automatically register and track every `MediaStream`.
   - On `releaseAllMediaResources()`:
     - Iterates through all active streams and calls `track.stop()` on every video and audio track (hardware camera LED and mic indicator immediately turn off).
     - Closes all active `AudioContext` instances.
     - Calls `destroySharedSdk()` to wind down the native SmartSpectra C-API engine.
   - Automatically wired to:
     - `window.onbeforeunload`, `window.onunload`, `window.onpagehide`
     - `window.onerror` (unhandled exceptions in window)
     - `window.onunhandledrejection` (unhandled promise rejections)
     - `app:will-close` (IPC from Electron main process)
2. **React Error Boundary Hardware Guard** ([ErrorBoundary.tsx](file:///Users/shivam/work/hotel-coach/src/components/common/ErrorBoundary.tsx#L35-L45)):
   - Added `releaseAllMediaResources()` inside `componentDidCatch`. If any React screen or component encounters a runtime error, all camera and microphone hardware tracks are shut off immediately.
3. **Electron Main Process Graceful Shutdown** ([main.cjs](file:///Users/shivam/work/hotel-coach/electron/main.cjs#L900-L950)):
   - Added `performGracefulShutdown()`:
     - Broadcasts `app:will-close` to all BrowserWindows so renderers immediately release media devices.
     - Shuts down background seeding worker threads (`seedOrchestrator.shutdown()`).
     - Performs synchronous emergency flush and closes the SQLite database (`storageManager.emergencyFlushSync()`, `storageManager.close()`).
   - Wired into:
     - `mainWindow.on("close")` & `mainWindow.on("closed")` (setting `mainWindow = null`).
     - `app.on("before-quit")` & `app.on("will-quit")`.
     - System process termination signals: `SIGINT` (Ctrl+C) and `SIGTERM`.

